## Phase 6 — Cloud metadata reference

| Provider | Base | Safe proof | Sensitive (describe, don't fetch) | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| AWS EC2 | `http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/` | `instance-id`, `hostname`, `ami-id`, `iam/security-credentials/` (role name) | `iam/security-credentials/<ROLE>`, `/latest/user-data` | IMDSv2 needs PUT token; also `http://instance-data/` |
| AWS ECS | `http://169.254.170.2/` | Reachability | `v2/credentials/<id>` | |
| GCP | `http://metadata.google.internal/computeMetadata/v1/` | `instance/id`, `instance/hostname`, `project/project-id` | `instance/service-accounts/default/token` | Needs `Metadata-Flavor: Google` |
| Azure | `http://169.254.169.254/metadata/instance?api-version=2021-02-01` | `compute/vmId`, `compute/name` | `identity/oauth2/token` | Needs `Metadata: true` |
| DigitalOcean | `http://169.254.169.254/metadata/v1/` | `id`, `hostname`, `region` | `user-data` | |
| Alibaba | `http://100.100.100.200/latest/meta-data/` | `instance-id`, `image-id` | `ram/security-credentials/`, user-data | |
| Oracle | `http://169.254.169.254/opc/v1/instance/` | `id`, `displayName` | — | v2 needs `Authorization: Bearer Oracle` |
| OpenStack | `http://169.254.169.254/openstack/latest/meta_data.json` | `uuid`, `name` | — | |
| Kubernetes | `https://kubernetes.default.svc/` | `/version` | Anything needing SA token | |

Example impact wording:
> The SSRF reaches AWS IMDS (IMDSv1). `/latest/meta-data/iam/security-credentials/` returned the role name `app-prod-role`. An attacker could request the next path for temporary credentials; I did not retrieve them per program rules. Impact depends on the role's permissions.

