## Phase 7 — Reporting

Keep impact claims tied to what was actually demonstrated. Precise reports get upgraded; overclaimed ones get downgraded.

```markdown
# SSRF in <feature> allows <what you reached>

## Summary
Endpoint, type (in-band / blind / semi-blind), highest-impact thing demonstrated.

## Affected asset
- URL / endpoint:
- Parameter / field:
- Auth required: yes/no
- Minimum role: <any self-signup user / paid plan / org admin>
- Fetch timing: immediate / on trigger (<what triggers it>) / scheduled (~<delay>)

## Steps to reproduce
1. Sign up / log in as <role>. Navigate to <Settings → Integrations → ...>.
2. Save / send the request below (tokens redacted).
3. Trigger the fetch: <click Test / wait N minutes / export report>.
4. Observe <response / OAST callback with timestamp / timing difference>.

    <exact raw HTTP request or curl>

## Evidence
- Callback log (source IP, timestamp, User-Agent) — source IP belongs to target
- Response excerpt (redacted)
- Screenshots

## Bypass used (if any)
e.g. "Filter blocks 127.0.0.1 but accepts decimal 2130706433."

## Impact
What you showed, then what it enables.

## Suggested severity
<rating> + CVSS vector if used. OWASP A10:2021.

## Remediation
(see Phase 8)
```

**Severity guide (illustrative — programs differ):**
| Demonstrated | Typical rating |
|---|---|
| DNS lookup only | Informative / P5 |
| HTTP callback from target infra | Low–Medium / P4 |
| Internal port/service reachability | Medium / P3 |
| Internal pages / unauthenticated internal APIs readable | High / P2 |
| Cloud metadata reachable, local file read | High–Critical / P2–P1 |

**Common reasons SSRF reports get closed:**
- Callback came from the tester's browser or a public link-preview bot.
- DNS-only, no HTTP.
- Feature is *meant* to fetch external URLs and nothing internal was reached.
- Testing went beyond scope (credential use, data modification) — can void the bounty.
- Authenticated report with unclear repro steps — triagers couldn't reach the feature or trigger the delayed fetch.
- Live session tokens pasted unredacted in the report.

