## Phase 8 — Remediation

- Allow-list destinations and schemes (http/https only); don't rely on regex or blacklists alone.
- Resolve the hostname, validate the resolved IP against private/loopback/link-local ranges (including IPv6 and mapped forms), then connect to **that same IP** (defeats rebinding).
- Disable automatic redirects, or re-validate every hop.
- Enforce egress restrictions at the network layer so app servers can't reach metadata or internal admin ports.
- AWS: require IMDSv2 with hop limit 1. GCP/Azure: rely on required metadata headers and block header injection.

